### Standalone CLI installation

<details>
<summary>Prebuilt installers (all features)</summary>
<br>

**Linux / macOS:**
```sh
curl -fsSL {{ $global.stub_url_sh }} | bash
```
Installs to `~/{{ $global.unix_default_suffix }}`. Set `INSTALL_DIR` to choose another destination.

**Windows (PowerShell, not Command Prompt):**
```powershell
(irm '{{ $global.stub_url_ps1 }}') | iex
```
Installs to `{{ $global.windows_default_prefix }}{{ $global.windows_default_suffix }}`, already on PATH. Set `$env:INSTALL_DIR` to choose another destination.

For a reproducible install, pin an explicit release:

```sh
(export VERSION=v{{ env:CRATE_VERSION }}; curl -fsSL {{ $global.stub_url_sh }} | bash)
```

```powershell
$env:VERSION = 'v{{ env:CRATE_VERSION }}'; (irm '{{ $global.stub_url_ps1 }}') | iex
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Install from source (Cargo)</summary>
<br>

**Build from source via Cargo** (same full module surface as the
release downloads: `NET`, `SSH`, `MARKDOWN`, plus `--mcp` hosting):

From the registry:

```sh
cargo install oxdock@{{ env:CRATE_VERSION }}
```

From a local checkout:

```sh
cargo install --path oxdock
```

</details>

### Add to Rust project

```sh
cargo add oxdock@{{ env:CRATE_VERSION }}
```
